<%- include('../partials/head', {
  title: 'Privacy Policy',
  canonicalPath: '/privacy',
  description: 'What information RYDJA collects when you request a quote, why we collect it, who we share it with, and how long we keep it.'
}) %>

<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="section shell narrow legal">
  <div class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</div>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="lede smaller">
    This describes what we collect when you ask us to quote a job, what we do with it, and what we do not do with it.
    It is written plainly because you should be able to tell at a glance.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>When you contact us or request a quote, we may collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name</li>
    <li>Your phone number</li>
    <li>Your email address, if you give us one</li>
    <li>The service or property address and access details</li>
    <li>Your description of the job</li>
    <li>Photographs you upload</li>
    <li>Preferred dates and times, and any scheduling notes</li>
    <li>For an estate or whole-property cleanout: which areas of the property are involved, roughly how much of it, and any deadline you tell us about</li>
    <li>Quote information: amounts, notes and whether you approved or declined</li>
    <li>Scheduling information: proposed and confirmed appointments, and your replies about them</li>
    <li>Questions or messages you send us through your job page</li>
    <li>Records of the work itself: status, dates, photographs taken on the job, and related job records</li>
    <li>
      How you found us: campaign labels carried in the web address of one of our own adverts or links, the website
      you came from (the domain only, such as <code>facebook.com</code>), and which of our pages you landed on first
    </li>
    <li>
      Limited technical information the site generates in the ordinary course of running and protecting itself, such
      as IP addresses used for rate limiting and records of refused or abusive requests
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your quote request</li>
    <li>To evaluate the job and work out what it involves</li>
    <li>To send you a quote</li>
    <li>To propose and confirm a time, and to schedule the work</li>
    <li>To perform the work you asked for</li>
    <li>To keep business and job records, including for accounting</li>
    <li>To see which of our own adverts and listings actually bring in work, so we stop paying for the ones that do not</li>
    <li>To prevent abuse, fraud and misuse of the site</li>
    <li>To operate, maintain and secure the website</li>
    <li>To meet legal and regulatory obligations</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Photographs</h2>
  <p>
    Photographs you send are used to assess the job, prepare your quote, plan the work, and document job conditions
    where that is operationally appropriate.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not use your photographs for advertising, marketing or social media.</strong> Uploading a photo does
    not give us permission to publish it. If we ever want to use one that way, we will ask you separately and
    explicitly, and you are free to say no.
  </p>

  <h2>We do not sell your information</h2>
  <p>
    RYDJA does not sell customer personal information, and does not share it with anyone for their own advertising or
    marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We use a small number of service providers to run the business. They receive only what they need to do their part,
    and they act on our instructions:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Website hosting</strong> &mdash; runs the site and stores its data</li>
    <li><strong>Transactional email</strong> &mdash; delivers your quote and appointment emails</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud backup and storage</strong> &mdash; holds encrypted-in-transit copies of business records so they survive a failure</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also share information where we are legally required to, or where it is reasonably necessary to protect
    the safety, rights or property of a person or of the business.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>This site runs no analytics, no advertising pixels, no session recording and no third-party tracking
    scripts.</strong> Nothing on these pages reports your visit to Google, Meta or anyone else, and nothing here can
    see where you go after you leave.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two cookies exist, both set by us and readable only by us. They are kept separate on purpose, and most people
    only ever receive the first:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Which link brought you here.</strong> If you arrived from one of our ads or posts, the web address
      carries campaign labels such as <code>utm_source=facebook</code>; we store those, the website address you came
      from &mdash; the domain only, never the page &mdash; and which of our pages you landed on first. That lets us
      see which adverts actually bring in work. <strong>It lasts 30 days from your first visit</strong>, so that if
      you come back later and ask for a quote we still know which advert to credit. It is written once and not
      renewed, so the 30 days runs from that first visit and not from the last time you looked. It holds nothing that
      identifies you and no record of when you visited.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A staff sign-in.</strong> Set only when a member of staff signs in to the administration area, to keep
      them signed in. Customers never receive it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This information says which link was clicked. It is not an identifier, it is not combined with anything bought
    from a data broker, it is not shared with an advertising network, and it is never used to build a profile of you
    or to follow you to another website.
  </p>

  <h2>Your job link</h2>
  <p>
    Each request gets a private page at a long, random, unguessable web address. Anyone who has that link can see that
    job, so treat it like you would any private link &mdash; it is the key to the page. Your permanent reference
    number, the one that looks like RYDJA-XXXXXX, is not a key and opens nothing on its own.
  </p>

  <h2>How we protect it</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable measures to protect the information we hold: access to the administration area is restricted
    and password protected, secrets are held in server configuration rather than in the code, uploads are validated,
    requests are rate limited, backups are taken, and customer names, phone numbers, addresses, email addresses and
    private job links are deliberately kept out of our server logs.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>No website, server or method of transmission is free of risk, and we cannot guarantee absolute
    security.</strong> Anyone who tells you otherwise about any system is overstating it. If you become aware of a
    security problem with this site, please tell us.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We collect what is reasonably necessary to quote and perform the work, and we keep records for as long as is
    reasonably needed for operational, accounting, legal, security and other legitimate business purposes. Backups are
    kept so the business can recover from a failure, and copies may persist in those backups for a period after a
    record changes.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This is a service for property owners and occupiers. It is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect information from them.</p>

  <h2>Questions, corrections and requests</h2>
  <p>
    If you want to know what we hold about you, have something corrected, or ask us to delete something, get in
    touch and we will do what we reasonably can.
    <% if (businessPhone) { %>Call or text <a class="text-link" href="tel:<%= telHref(businessPhone) %>"><%= businessPhone %></a><% } %><% if (businessEmail) { %><% if (businessPhone) { %>, or email<% } else { %>Email<% } %> <a class="text-link" href="mailto:<%= businessEmail %>"><%= businessEmail %></a><% } %>.
    Some records we may need to keep for accounting or legal reasons.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes we will update the date below. Material changes will be reflected here rather than announced by email.</p>

  <p class="legal-foot">Last updated: October 2026</p>
</main>

<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
